{"kind":"stack","id":"sound-vibrations","title":"Sound and vibrations: how sound travels to the ear","theme":{"background":"#f4f9ff","foreground":"#1d2b3a","font":"Comic Sans MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Vibration"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A quick back-and-forth shaking movement. Sounds are made by vibrations."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Medium"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"The material sound travels through, such as air, water or solid objects."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What is made when an object vibrates?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A sound","why":"Vibrations travel to the ear and are heard as sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A shadow","why":"Pupils may confuse shadows, which come from blocked light, with sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A colour","why":"Pupils may mix up senses and think sight-related things come from sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Through what can sound travel to reach your ear?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"A medium such as air","why":"Sound needs a medium like air, water or solids to travel through.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Empty space with nothing in it","why":"Pupils may think sound travels through nothing, but it needs a medium.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Only through light","why":"Pupils may confuse light and sound, which travel differently.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"You hear a drum in the next room. Do you press your ear to the wall or walk closer to the door?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Press your ear to the wall","why":"A solid wall carries vibrations to your ear.","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Walk closer to the door","why":"The air carries vibrations to you.","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The drum sounds loud through the solid wall. Solids carry vibrations well."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Through the air, the drum sounds clear. Air is a medium for sound."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"What does your ear do with sound vibrations?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Passes them on to the brain as sound","why":"The ear picks up vibrations and sends signals to the brain.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Stores them for later","why":"Pupils may think the ear keeps sounds like a recording.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Makes them stronger by itself","why":"Pupils may think the ear adds energy to sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which material carries sound vibrations best?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"A solid such as wood","why":"Solids carry vibrations better than air, which is why the wall sounded loud.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"A vacuum with no particles","why":"Pupils may think nothing at all is needed, but sound cannot travel through a vacuum.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Light from a torch","why":"Pupils may confuse light with a medium for sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"When you speak, what starts the sound?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Your vocal cords vibrating","why":"Vocal cords vibrate and make the air around them vibrate.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Your lips closing tightly","why":"Pupils may think lips alone make sound, but the vibration starts in the throat.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Your tongue touching your teeth","why":"Pupils may think the tongue makes all sound, but the vibration starts in the throat.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done: you finished sound and vibrations"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Sound travels as vibrations through a medium to your ear. Great work today."}],"actions":[]}}
